      ],
      "known_issue": "This upstream file is a work in progress: it references several signals (tmp_read_data, tmp_error, key0_reg, ...) that it never declares, so it does not elaborate standalone under Icarus even with every sibling module supplied. It is deliberately retained in the corpus because it exercises the pipeline's advisory-mode path -- Phase 4 logs 'annotated_input_does_not_compile', downgrades the per-step syntax gate to advisory, and still produces a transformed deliverable, and Phase 5 reports the resulting FAIL honestly rather than hiding it."
